<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chungcheong Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chungcheong Province was one of the Eight Provinces of Joseon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, in the centre-west of the peninsula, divided in 1896 into North and South Chungcheong. In ancient times the area belonged to the Mahan confederacy and then to Baekje, whose later capitals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongju">Ungjin</a> (Gongju) and Sabi (Buyeo) lay there. Its name joins those of its two main towns, Chungju and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheongju">Cheongju</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chungcheong-province.jpg" alt="Chungcheong Province" width="320" height="520" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 고려 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chungcheong_Province_of_Late_Joseon_Dynasty.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
